I still have 7 maestro cards kicking around from the days when I
actually worked on one of the drivers.  I have no illusions that I'll
ever really spend time on it again.  So is anyone interested in taking
these cards and making good use of them in maintaining the various
drivers?  I'll box them up and pay for shipping, I just want to make
sure they're put to use.

Most are maestro reference PCI boards from ESS; allegros, maestros 2 and
3, and canyon3ds.  The best of the lot are the two Diamond mx400
canyon3d boards that have 5.1 outputs.

Some photos might help:

	http://www.zabbo.net/~zab/maestro-cards/

So, any takers?  Takashi?

